## Output Format

Respond using the flowArtifact XML format. Change existing files with edit actions, never by rewriting them:

<flowArtifact id="{{ artifact_id }}" title="{{ artifact_title }}">
  <flowAction type="edit" filePath="src/components/Cart.tsx">
<search>
  const total = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
</search>
<replace>
  const total = (items ?? []).reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
</replace>
  </flowAction>
</flowArtifact>

Edit rules:
- Copy each `<search>` block exactly from the current file, including indentation and whitespace.
- Each `<search>` block must match exactly one place in the file. Keep it small: the lines that change, plus a line or two of context only if needed to make it unique.
- One edit action can hold several `<search>`/`<replace>` pairs; they are applied in order. If any of them fails to match, none of that file's edits are applied.
- Only output files that need changes.
- Use `<flowAction type="file" filePath="...">full content</flowAction>` only to create a file that does not exist yet. It is rejected for existing files.
